E2E TESTING (LOCAL) - zkx402 / x402 middleware

Quick run (one command):
- cd apps/demo/local-chain
- node run-e2e-test.js

What the runner does:
- Starts Anvil on :8545 (if not already running)
- Deploys MockUSDC (EIP-3009 transferWithAuthorization enabled)
- Mints 10,000 USDC to the test payer
- Writes server env file: apps/demo/server/.env.local
- Starts server: apps/demo/server/index.js
- Runs client test: apps/demo/local-chain/test-e2e.js

If port 3001 is already in use:
- lsof -ti:3001 | xargs -r kill -9

If Anvil is already running and you want a clean chain:
- pkill -f anvil

Key files:
- apps/demo/local-chain/run-e2e-test.js     (orchestrates full E2E)
- apps/demo/local-chain/test-e2e.js         (client flow)
- apps/demo/server/index.js                 (server; loads .env.local and uses local facilitator)
- apps/demo/local-chain/local-facilitator.js (local verify + settle via transferWithAuthorization)
- apps/demo/contracts/src/MockUSDC.sol      (Mock USDC with EIP-3009 transferWithAuthorization)

Important details:
- The X-PAYMENT header must match the `x402` npm package schema:
  { x402Version, scheme, network, payload: { signature, authorization: { from, to, value, validAfter, validBefore, nonce } } }
- The `x402-zkx402` middleware imports from the `x402` npm package (not @coinbase/x402 subpaths).
- In this repo, Node 24 can cause native dependency builds to fail; prefer installs with:
  npm install --ignore-scripts --legacy-peer-deps

